# SDD Governance Build Rules

## Repository Context

This repository is a CUAD contract review and risk-flagging pipeline.

Its current function is:

- ingest CUAD contracts
- extract legal clause spans
- compare clauses against a legal playbook
- assign risk severity
- generate plain-English summaries
- write execution logs and audit reports

Do not replace the existing contract-review pipeline.

## Target Architecture

Add a governance layer using this framing:

- SDD as the governance methodology
- Policy-as-code as the enforcement layer
- CI/CD as the execution layer
- Audit reports as the evidence layer

## Build Goal

Create an SDD-inspired governance layer that validates whether the contract-review pipeline, agents, risk outputs, logs, reports, and repo structure conform to machine-readable governance specs.

The governance layer should not replace the existing ExtractionAgent, RiskAgent, SummaryAgent, CLI, Streamlit dashboard, or tests.

## Required Structure

Create or adapt the following structure:

governance/
  specs/
    agent-governance.spec.yaml
    pipeline-governance.spec.yaml
    audit-governance.spec.yaml
    ci-governance.spec.yaml
  policies/
    repo_policy.yaml
    agent_policy.yaml
    audit_policy.yaml
  validators/
    spec_loader.py
    repo_validator.py
    agent_validator.py
    pipeline_validator.py
    audit_validator.py
  reports/
    governance_report.py
  models.py
  validate.py

## Requirements

The governance layer must validate:

- required files exist
- required folders exist
- tests exist
- sensitive files are not considered safe for agent editing
- agents are named and documented
- risk outputs include severity and reason
- summaries include traceability to risk findings
- audit logs are expected outputs
- high and critical findings require human review status
- governance reports are generated as evidence

## CLI Requirement

Add a simple command such as:

python -m governance.validate

or:

python governance/validate.py

Choose the least disruptive option.

## CI/CD Requirement

Add or update GitHub Actions so the repo can:

- install dependencies
- run tests
- run governance validation
- fail on critical governance failures
- avoid deployment

## Testing Requirement

Add tests for:

- loading governance specs
- loading policies
- validating required files
- validating sensitive paths
- generating governance reports
- full governance pass case
- full governance failure case

Do not remove existing tests.

## Documentation Requirement

Update README.md to explain:

- what the SDD governance layer does
- how SDD acts as the methodology
- how policy-as-code enforces requirements
- how CI/CD executes checks
- how audit reports provide evidence
- how to run the governance validator

## Token Efficiency

Do not repeatedly reread the same files.

First inspect:

- README.md
- requirements.txt
- main.py
- dashboard.py
- report_builder.py
- src/
- tests/
- .github/workflows/ if present

Then create:

docs/CURSOR_WORKING_NOTES.md

Use that file to summarize the project and avoid repeatedly rereading unchanged files.

## Non-Goals

Do not add Firecrawl, MCP, Langflow, or Dify in this task.

Do not convert the project to LangChain, AutoGen, or a heavy agent framework.

Do not hardcode local Windows paths into reusable source code.

Do not break the existing Streamlit dashboard or CLI.

## Definition of Done

The task is complete when:

- governance specs exist
- policy files exist
- validators execute
- governance report is generated
- tests pass
- README is updated
- GitHub Actions can run tests and governance validation
- existing CUAD contract-review functionality still works
